From: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>
Subject: [PATCH] render the page without the GPU

On the receiver chromium's GPU rendering crashes the GL driver with the
effects some applications use (ZDF, a few seconds after its video
starts); rendered in software the page is shown through Qt only.
---
diff --git a/main.cpp b/main.cpp
index 32ff26c..6fb7006 100644
--- a/main.cpp
+++ b/main.cpp
@@ -67,6 +67,12 @@ int main(int argc, char *argv[])
     // the browser runs as root, where chromium refuses its sandbox
     if (qgetenv("QTWEBENGINE_DISABLE_SANDBOX").isNull())
         qputenv("QTWEBENGINE_DISABLE_SANDBOX", "1");
+    // chromium's GPU rendering crashes the GL driver of the receiver with
+    // the effects of some applications (ZDF when its video starts); the
+    // page is rendered in software and only shown through Qt
+    QByteArray chromiumFlags = qgetenv("QTWEBENGINE_CHROMIUM_FLAGS");
+    if (!chromiumFlags.split(' ').contains("--disable-gpu"))
+        qputenv("QTWEBENGINE_CHROMIUM_FLAGS", (chromiumFlags + " --disable-gpu").trimmed());
 #endif
 
     QCoreApplication::setOrganizationName(QLatin1String("Qt"));
